; One warning, at the reference — not at either declaration. Both
; declarations are individually fine; it is the *reference* that has two
; readings, so that is where the repair decision is made (rename one
; declaration, or split the slot into two single-kind keys).
;
; Pathed at the value like the rest of the post-match advisory family
; (`deprecated_member`, `string_pattern_unsupported`), and `warning`
; severity so the document still validates.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code union_ambiguous :severity warning :path [dispatch pipeline]))
